WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.870
High on Mauna Loa, scientists measure
the carbon dioxide in the air.

2
00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:09.010
Each northern summer, as
plants grow, the level falls.

3
00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:12.910
Each winter, as leaves
decay, it rises again.

4
00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:18.150
Before the Industrial Revolution, carbon
dioxide stood at 280 parts per million

5
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:19.550
or less.

6
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:22.910
Through the ice-age cycles of
the past million years or so,

7
00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.290
it never rose above 300.

8
00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:28.980
So why did the air's carbon
stay level for millennia?

9
00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:33.530
In this mission, you'll model the
water and carbon cycles as systems,

10
00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:38.090
with stores, flows,
inputs, outputs and energy.

11
00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:42.810
Then you'll divide a store by its flow,
and find out how long water stays in the

12
00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:43.690
air.

13
00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:48.270
Your mission: explain how the carbon
in the air held steady for millennia.
